# Nothing in this directory is ever fetched over HTTP. It holds application code
# that pages under the web root include from disk.
#
# This exists because the deploy rsyncs sites/reporting/ wholesale into the web
# root, so app/ lands under DocumentRoot whether or not that was intended. PHP
# files would normally be executed rather than disclosed, but a misconfiguration
# that stops PHP from handling .php (a broken FPM socket, a bad handler change)
# turns every one of these into a plain-text download containing the auth logic.
#
# Belt and braces: each file also refuses to run unless CSE135_APP is defined, so
# losing this .htaccess is not on its own sufficient to expose anything.
Require all denied
